# __APP_DISPLAY_NAME__

Standalone Hudson consumer client scaffolded by `create-hudson-app --tier standalone`.

> **Scope:** Vite + TanStack Router for **standalone consumer clients** only.
> Hudson monorepo product surfaces stay on Next.js. Do not treat this template
> as the path for in-repo apps (`app/apps/*`).

## Stack

| Piece | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| Bundler | Vite (`base: './'` for file / WKWebView hosts) |
| Router | TanStack Router (scaffold point) |
| UI kit | `hudsonkit` AppShell + `hudsonkit/nav` + `hudsonkit/behaviors` |
| Typecheck | `tsc --noEmit` **before** `vite build` (`bun run check`) |
| Theme | Seed → full token set via `src/theme-adapter.ts` (edge ≠ ink) |

## Commands

```bash
bun install
bun run dev        # http://127.0.0.1:5173
bun run typecheck
bun run check      # typecheck && build
bun run test       # theme adapter guard
```

## hudsonkit dependency (pre-publish)

This template targets **hudsonkit ≥ 0.4.0** (AppShell, `hudsonkit/nav`,
`hudsonkit/behaviors`, styles type decls). Until that version is on npm,
point at a local pack from the Hudson monorepo:

```bash
# from packages/web/hudsonkit in the hudson repo
bun run pack   # emits hudsonkit-0.4.0.tgz (exact version from package.json)

# in this app
bun add hudsonkit@file:/absolute/path/to/hudsonkit-0.4.0.tgz
```

When scaffolding from inside the Hudson monorepo, `create-hudson-app` auto-wires
`file:` to the monorepo pack matching `packages/web/hudsonkit/package.json`
version when that tarball is present (set `HUDSONKIT_TGZ=/path/to.tgz` to override).

## Layout

- `/` — AppShell destinations rail + content (SPA)
- `/embeds/*.html` — optional multi-entry embeds (uncomment in `vite.config.ts`)
- `/broker/*` — Vite dev proxy to local broker (`HUDSON_BROKER_URL`, default `:43110`)

During local development, fetch the broker via same-origin `/broker/...` —
never hit `:43110` from the browser (no CORS). Configure an equivalent
same-origin proxy in the production host; `vite preview` does not provide it.

## Theme rule (load-bearing)

`--border` / `--input` **must** derive from edge channels, never ink.
`src/theme-adapter.test.ts` fails the build story if that regression returns.

## Package safety

The generated package remains `private: true` to prevent accidental npm
publishing. Run `bun run check` before treating it as a consumer baseline.
